# reranker-__name__

A reranker that keeps the order it was given: the smallest correct one, as `./engine plugin new reranker <name>`
writes it. Make it read the search and each candidate's text, and score how well the candidate answers.

## Use it

```ts
// engine.config.ts
import { defineEngine } from "@louvain/engine-core";
import { __camelName__ } from "@louvain/reranker-__name__";

export default defineEngine({ reranker: __camelName__() });
```

## Make it yours

This is the whole of `src/index.ts`:

```ts
import { definePlugin } from "@louvain/engine-core";
import { z } from "zod";

export const __camelName__ = definePlugin({
  kind: "reranker",
  name: "__name__",
  settings: z.object({}),
  create: () => ({
    model: "__name__",
    rerank: async ({ texts }) => ({ ok: true, scores: texts.map((_, i) => 1 / (i + 1)) }),
  }),
});
```

1. **`definePlugin`** makes a factory; `engine.config.ts` calls it. A configuration runs one reranker, or none.
2. **`settings`** is a zod schema for what the configuration passes, such as a URL, a model or a timeout. A wrong
   setting stops the start with the schema's own message. Read a key from the environment in its default, so it is
   never written into a file.
3. **`model`** names what makes the scores: a cut-off measured on one model is never applied to another's. A reranker
   may also state `cutoffs` (`{ matched }`: at or above it, a document matches) and `blend` (how much of the order is
   its own, from 0 to 1).
4. **`rerank`** gets `{ query, texts }` and returns one score from 0 to 1 per text, in the order asked, as
   `{ ok: true, scores }`. A reranker that cannot answer returns `{ ok: false, failure: "<why>" }`; it never throws,
   and the engine then keeps the order it had and says the search was not reranked.

Test it through the registry, as `test/index.test.ts` does. `packages/plugins/reranker-cohere` is a complete one that
calls an API.
